<title>UK: UK notes in circulation rise 5.6 pct in week.</title>
<headline>UK notes in circulation rise 5.6 pct in week.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>British bank notes in circulation rose 5.6 percent in the week to July 16 over the equivalent week a year ago, figures from the Bank of England showed. Last week the rise was 6.3 percent.</p>
<p>(figures in rounded billions of stg) -</p>
<p>		     Latest week  Previous week year-ago week</p>
<p> Notes in circulation  21.79    21.81     20.63</p>
<p> Bankers deposits	 2.65     2.58	1.92</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7715</p>
</text>
